00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:37.120
metric as our silver bullet, like bundle&nbsp;
size or time to first byte from our CDN.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:45.120
In reality, as projects progress we inevitably&nbsp;
discover significant challenges below, like fonts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:52.240
images, chat widgets, YouTube embeds, and many&nbsp;
other third-party scripts. To tackle this, Next.js&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:58.720
follows two main strategies. First, great defaults&nbsp;
for production that are applied automatically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:03.920
such as optimizing JS bundles and inlining
the critical CSS of the fonts you're using.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.680
Second, building on the powerful React&nbsp;
abstractions, we give you drop-in replacements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:15.440
for common needs that you can implement to get&nbsp;
better performance. For snappy navigation with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.640
the benefits of a single-page application, Next.js&nbsp;
took the "a" tag and gave you the link component.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.680
With automatic prefetching combined with&nbsp;
pre-rendering, Next.js gives you the best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:32.800
of both worlds: great seo and instant client-side&nbsp;
transitions. For image tags, we gave you the image&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:38.640
component. Just as easy to use plus automatic&nbsp;
resizing for different viewports, non-blocking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.680
rendering, and beautiful transitions from a&nbsp;
blurred image into its final optimized state.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:49.600
For script tags, we gave you the script&nbsp;
component with easy to use strategies to prevent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.440
third-party scripts from getting in the&nbsp;
way of critical interactions on your page,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.080 --> 00:03:00.160
like signing up for your service or buying an item&nbsp;
on your store. We recognize that try to memorize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:06.720
all of these best practices is unproductive, so&nbsp;
last June at the Special Edition of Next.js Conf&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:13.760
we shipped built-in conformance. With conformance,&nbsp;
if you forget to use any of these tools, Next.js&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:20.960
will remind you and help you and your team ship&nbsp;
better applications. Great production defaults and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:26.480
great built-in components, plus the conformance&nbsp;
to reinforce them, has delivered in a great way.

